%%{init: {'theme': 'neutral', 'themeVariables': {'fontFamily': 'Inter, system-ui', 'lineWidth': '2'}}}%%
%% Title: Postrun Retention Deduplication And Vacuum Warning Path
%% @version 1.1.0
%% @date    2026-10-09
%% Reviewed against main 9a7339dc: storage/support/retention.py, retention_dedup.py; core/postrun/compact_orchestrator.py
%% @type    sequenceDiagram
%% @level   System / Interaction
%% @nodes   6
%% RULES: RULES.md §2.1, §2.8, ADR-013, ADR-014
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Runner as PipelineRunner / postrun
    participant Builder as build_postrun_service
    participant Service as PostrunCompactService
    participant Retention as retention.py
    participant Delta as runtime_delta_table
    participant Warn as warning allowlist

    Builder->>Service: construct with warning allowlist
    Builder-->>Runner: service
    Runner->>Service: execute postrun tasks
    Note over Service,Retention: Compaction applies to APPEND / MERGE with table and primary keys
    Service->>Retention: storage.deduplicate_silver(table, primary_keys)
    Retention->>Retention: _resolve_deduplication_timeout_seconds()
    alt test_mode and configured timeout at least 60 seconds
        Retention->>Retention: 10 seconds on other platforms / 60 on Windows
    else smaller custom timeout or normal mode
        Retention->>Retention: keep configured value
    end
    Retention->>Delta: to_pyarrow_dataset().scanner().head(row_count)
    alt dedup succeeds
        Delta-->>Retention: rows
        Retention-->>Service: duplicates removed
        Service->>Retention: storage.optimize(table)
    else TimeoutError
        Delta-->>Retention: timeout
        Service->>Warn: check allowlist
        Warn-->>Service: log warning and return CompactionResult failed
    end
    Note over Service,Warn: Errors outside the allowlist propagate; vacuum is a separate retention operation
    Service-->>Runner: success / skipped / failed result
